i></ul></span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Responding to request:</span> <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>For sure.</li> <li>Sure, I'd love to.</li> <li>Yeah, no problem.</li></ul></span>"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "backed up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "describes the situation when there is a long line of people or cars"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are often cars backed up on the highway."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob01aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about travel and transportation."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to bum around"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to go to various places with a friend, to hang out"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Peter wants to bum around Boston for the day with Sally."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob01aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to venture"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to go to some place new or unfamiliar"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Peter ventured into Boston months ago."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob01aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "brilliant"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "refers to a good idea"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's brilliant to take the train into the city instead of driving."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le15ob01aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "scenic"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "describing nice scenery or views from the train, car or the top of a 